  "summary_en": "UK Government white paper and consultation proposing a non-statutory, context-based, regulator-led approach to AI. Five cross-sectoral principles (safety, transparency, fairness, accountability, contestability) are applied by existing regulators, supported by central functions, sandboxes, assurance tools and international interoperability. Self-driving vehicles and medical devices appear only as brief examples.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Five non-statutory cross-sectoral principles implemented by existing regulators",
   "Possible future statutory duty on regulators to have due regard to the principles",
   "No new AI regulator; central functions for monitoring, risk assessment, horizon scanning",
   "Context-based regulation of AI use rather than the technology, defined by adaptivity and autonomy",
   "Regulatory sandbox, assurance tools, technical standards and international interoperability"
